    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d357">

                <pb facs="0453" n="443" sameAs="frus:frus1947v07/pg443"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/3–3147: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in the
                        Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Smith</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-04-02T19:00:00-05:00">April 2, 1947—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>775. For the Secretary<anchor n="21" xml:id="d357-f1"/> from Acheson.<anchor
                        n="22" xml:id="d357-f2"/> We suggest awaiting receipt of despatch 588 March
                    26 containing concrete proposals on Formosa (Nanking’s 689 March 29) before
                    preparing reply to Stuart (Kosmos 17)<anchor n="23" xml:id="d357-f3"/> In
                    meantime we are studying available materials on subject. Assistance in economic
                    development of Formosa appears sound in principle but at first blush we question
                    practicability of sending technical advisers without reasonable prospect of
                    supporting credits.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d357-f1" n="21" xml:id="d357-f1-content">
                <p>The Secretary of State was at this time attending the Moscow Conference of
                    Foreign Ministers.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d357-f2" n="22" xml:id="d357-f2-content">
                <p>Dean Acheson, Under Secretary of State.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d357-f3" n="23" xml:id="d357-f3-content">
                <p>For Ambassador Stuart’s despatch No. 588 and telegram No. 689, see <ref
                        target="#pg84">pp. 84</ref> and <ref target="#pg89">89</ref>, respectively.
                    Telegram Kosmos 17 (Moscow Embassy telegram No. 1109), March 31, 5 p.m., from
                    the Secretary of State to Mr. Acheson, not printed (711.93/3–3147); in it the
                    Secretary requested the Department’s recommended reply to Dr. Stuart’s request
                    for guidance made in the above cited telegram No. 689. In telegram No. 444,
                    April 17, 6 p.m., Mr. Acheson informed Dr. Stuart that his despatch No. 588 had
                    been received “and is now being studied by appropriate officers of Dept.”.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
